Subject: [PATCH] agent, library: a dsh patch list that opens with a YAML
 document start marker is edited, the marker kept

What changed
- dshParse (internal/agent/dsh.go) and dshRead (internal/library/dsh.go)
  let a patch list open with "---", YAML's document start marker: it goes
  in the head and is written back with it, where before it failed the file
  as "not a list of entries magpie can edit" (#2667).

Run
- Red on e085d6e9 with the new tests over a baseline copy (product files
  at HEAD): TestDshDocStart and TestDshDocStartPatchList fail with the
  reported "cordis.patch.yml is not a list of entries magpie can edit".
- Green with the fix: TestDshDocStart, TestDshDocStartPatchList, and the
  whole of internal/sessions, internal/provider, internal/agent and
  internal/library under -tags nogui -p 2.
- gofmt -l internal/agent internal/library: clean. go vet -tags nogui for
  darwin/arm64, linux/amd64 and windows/amd64: clean. go build for the
  three: ok (trayimage_darwin.go's cgo warning is on the base commit).
- Not run: the Playwright tests under internal/gui/tests.

